<Layout title="Privacy & cookies | MINA"><article class="wrap prose"><p class="eyebrow">WEBSITE INFORMATION</p><h1>Privacy & cookies</h1><p>Last updated: 26 September 2026</p><p>This notice concerns the informational website of MINA Consulting and Engineering LLC-FZ, Meydan Grandstand, 6th Floor, Meydan Road, Naad Al Sheba, Dubai, United Arab Emirates. For privacy enquiries, email <a href="mailto:info@mina-consulting.com">info@mina-consulting.com</a>.</p><h2>Browsing this website</h2><p>This website has no accounts, contact forms, analytics, advertising, tracking pixels or third-party embeds. The site does not set cookies or use browser storage. Images and styling are served with the website; no external font services are used.</p><h2>Hosting and technical information</h2><p>Serving a website requires the hosting service to receive technical information, including your IP address and requested pages. During local development, the preview server may log requests. The published website is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs visitors’ IP addresses for security purposes, even when they are not signed in. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a> for its handling of technical information, retention and international processing.</p><h2>Contacting MINA</h2><p>Email links open your own email application. If you contact us, we receive the information you choose to share, such as your name, contact details and enquiry. We use it to respond, discuss requested services and manage the resulting business correspondence. Please avoid sending sensitive personal information in an initial enquiry.</p><p>Where the GDPR applies, responding to a request for services may be necessary to take steps before entering a contract. Other ordinary business correspondence may be handled on the basis of our legitimate interest in responding to enquiries; legal obligations may require particular records to be kept. The applicable basis depends on the enquiry and relevant law.</p><h2>Access, retention and international processing</h2><p>Business correspondence may be handled by authorised personnel and service providers supporting communications. MINA is based in the UAE, and contacting us may involve processing there or in countries used by relevant service providers. We retain correspondence as needed for its purpose and applicable legal obligations. Specific retention periods and any required international transfer arrangements depend on the services and records involved; contact us for details.</p><h2>Your privacy rights</h2><p>Depending on applicable law, you may have rights to access, correct, erase or obtain a copy of your personal information, restrict or object to processing, or withdraw consent where processing relies on consent. You may also complain to the relevant data protection authority. To make a request about information held by MINA, use the email address above. We may need to verify your identity before responding.</p><h2>Changes</h2><p>This notice will be updated if the website’s features or data practices change.</p></article></Layout>
